You have **two methods with the same signature**:

- `DeleteConfirmed(string id)` at line ~38 (soft delete)
- `DeleteConfirmed(string id)` at line ~153 (hard delete)

That causes:

- `CS0111: already defines a member called 'DeleteConfirmed' with the same parameter types`

Keep only one `DeleteConfirmed` method.  
Delete the old hard-delete version (the one that calls `_context.Assets.Remove(asset)`).

The other message is only a warning (`#warning` in `YourDatabaseContext.cs`), not the build break.

If you want, use this as the single delete action:


```csharp
[HttpPost, ActionName("Delete")]
